  "releaseNotes": "Bug Fixes:\n- preserve local state and classify fenced deactivation\n  Keep State and HasUnsavedChanges readable during shutdown after a storage\n  failure while continuing to fence assignments, storage operations, and hook\n  configuration. Retain the published snapshot without adopting a failed write\n  candidate, following Orleans journaling's fence-and-deactivate behavior.\n  Reuse the existing write and clear classifiers for both recovery policies.\n  Subsequent rejected operations throw StateManagerFencedException with the\n  failure kind and original storage exception. Deactivation reasons retain the\n  original error and identify the state type, operation, and classification.\n  Record fencing on the grain context so readable snapshots do not conceal an\n  uncertain durable outcome. Outbox deactivation leaves reminders unchanged for\n  confirmed conflicts and ensures recovery for other fenced outcomes. Multiple\n  state failures cannot let a conflict hide uncertain work. Reminder warnings\n  include the observed outbox count, or null when the accessor cannot be read.\n  Document the consumer migration and cover retained snapshots, late storage\n  completion, classified failures, serialization, and real grain deactivation.\n  Keep deactivation independent of failure-recording errors in custom grain\n  contexts. Recorded fencing still drives outbox recovery when local inspection\n  throws an unrelated exception. Give the fencing exception a stable Orleans\n  serialization alias and document stale or unsaved reads before deactivation\n  finishes, including migration guidance for read-only grain methods.",
